ting debt refinanced in-year. Treasury investments fell to \u00a349.875m (from \u00a361.621m) \u2014 described as 'broadly at the council's liquidity buffer', the minimum cash its strategy allows \u2014 and the report acknowledges managing 'relatively low cash balances' through a volatile rate environment. Outside the treasury book sit \u00a3422.731m of non-treasury investments, including loans to council-owned subsidiaries, third-party developers and community organisations, plus gilts held against Brent Cross Plot 1 commercial agreements. Loan-level detail, the CFR and the maturity ladder are in Appendix A, presented with the outturn to Cabinet on 9 June 2026.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s95465/Treasury Outturn 2025-2026 - Cover Report to GARMS.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-06-11","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"\u00a3159.44m borrowed in 2025/26, taking total debt from \u00a31.157bn to \u00a31.317bn (+14%), the second year of heavy external borrowing since the internal-funding era ended in 2024/25","why":"Barnet has become a large, recurring borrower whose capital programme now depends on continuous access to PWLB and market debt."},{"code":"low-liquidity","headline":"Treasury investments of \u00a349.875m at 31 March 2026 were 'broadly at the council's liquidity buffer' \u2014 the lowest cash holding its strategy permits \u2014 down from \u00a361.621m a year earlier","why":"Sitting at the floor means any cash-flow shock converts directly into new short-term borrowing."},{"code":"company-exposure","headline":"\u00a3422.731m of non-treasury investments outstanding at 31 March 2026, including loans to local-authority-owned subsidiaries, third-party developers and community organisations","why":"A sum equal to a third of the council's debt is lent outside the treasury strategy's safeguards, with repayment resting on developers' and subsidiaries' performance."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a31.317bn total borrowing, up from \u00a31.157bn at end 2024/25 after \u00a3159.44m of new borrowing in 2025/26","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":1},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a349.875m treasury investments (31 March 2025: \u00a361.621m)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":1},{"name":"liquidity buffer","value":"\u00a349.875m was 'broadly at the council's liquidity buffer' \u2014 the lowest cash holding permitted by the Treasury Management Strategy Statement","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"company lending","value":"\u00a3422.731m non-treasury investments: loans to community organisations, third-party developers and local-authority-owned subsidiaries","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"net borrowing movement","value":"net borrowing up \u00a3122.74m for the General Fund and \u00a337.10m for the HRA in 2025/26","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":2},{"name":"refinanced debt","value":"\u00a349.36m of debt refinanced during 2025/26","as_at":"2025/26","page":2}],"commercial":{"company_lending":{"value":"\u00a3422.731m non-treasury investments: loans to community organisations, third-party developers and local-authority-owned subsidiaries","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3,"doc":"Treasury Management Outturn 2025/26"}},"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"Appendix A - Capital Programme 1","url":"http://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96136/appendix-a-capital-programme-1.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"21/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix B - Bad Debt Write Offs","url":"http://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96137/appendix-b-bad-debt-write-offs.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"21/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Chief Finance Officer Report - Outturn - F&G OSSC - with Clearances","url":"http://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96103/chief-finance-officer-report-outturn-f-g-ossc-with-clearance.pdf","committee":"Finance and Growth Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Committee","date":"20