moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Pension Fund Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Adults and Health Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-18","committee":"Joint Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Barnet borrowing \u00a373m for day-to-day costs as Q1 spending runs over budget","lead":"Barnet council is using exceptional financial support, a last-resort government measure allowing councils to borrow to cover day-to-day spending, with \u00a373.3m deployed to finance revenue costs. Revenue spending is running ahead of budget in the first quarter, with an additional \u00a32.621m overspend forecast on top of planned reserve usage of \u00a32.324m. The council also raised \u00a325m of temporary borrowing to support short-term cash flow. Meanwhile, audit recommendations remain unimplemented: only 55% of actions followed up in the first quarter were completed, against a target of 90%, a gap the Head of Internal Audit has flagged as material to the council's control environment.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"GARMS Report Internal Audit Q1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96822/96822.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","paper_title":"Appendix A - Treasury Management Performance Update Report \u2013 Q1 2627","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96826/96826.pdf","headline":"\u00a325m temporary borrowing raised in Q1 to support short-term cash flow","detail":"The council raised \u00a325m of temporary borrowing from the local authority market during Q1 2026/27 to support 'the Council's short-term cash flow requirements'. This temporary borrowing increased total debt from \u00a31.317bn to \u00a31.339bn.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Reliance on temporary borrowing for routine cash flow suggests the council's liquid reserves or payment timing are tighter than normal","figures":"\u00a325m temporary borrowing; total debt increased to \u00a31.339bn","quote":"\u00a325 million of temporary borrowing was raised from the local authority market to support the Council's short-term cash flow requirements","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","paper_title":"Appendix A - Treasury Management Performance Update Report \u2013 Q1 2627","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96826/96826.pdf","headline":"Q1 revenue overspend of \u00a32.621m in addition to planned reserve usage","detail":"The reserves forecast notes that planned reserve usage of \u00a32.324m 'does not include additional cash required to cover forecasted overspend of \u00a32.621m at Quarter 1'. Revenue spending is running ahead of budget in the first quarter, on top of planned reserve draws.","category":"overspend","matters":"Q1 overspend suggests the full-year budget may be underfunded, requiring further reserve drawdown or additional emergency financing beyond what was forecast","figures":"\u00a32.621m Q1 overspend; \u00a32.324m baseline reserve usage","quote":"\u00a32.324m expected usage does not include additional cash required to cover forecasted overspend of \u00a32.621m at Quarter 1","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","paper_title":"Appendix A - Treasury Management Performance Update Report \u2013 Q1 2627","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96826/96826.pdf","headline":"\u00a373.3m exceptional financial support being used to finance revenue costs","detail":"The Q1 capital financing forecast shows \u00a373.298m (44% of General Fund borrowing) is classified as 'Capitalisation Directive/Exceptional Finance Support (EFS) (Revenue)'. This means the council is borrowing to cover day-to-day operational spending rather than capital investment, indicating structural revenue pressures.","category":"overspend","matters":"Using EFS to borrow for revenue indicates the council cannot balance its day-to-day budget and is relying on temporary exceptional measures to cover the shortfall","figures":"\u00a373.298m out of \u00a3164.901m General Fund borrowing requirement","quote":"Capitalisation Directive/ Exceptional Finance Support (EFS) (Revenue) 73,298","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","paper_title":"Appendix A - Internal Audit Q1 2026-27 progress report","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96823/96823.pdf","headline":"The Barnet Group housing company has three high-risk audit findings including failure to meet Awaab's Law compliance timescales","detail":"An internal audit of The Barnet Group (the council-owned housing company) identified three high-risk and two medium-risk findings on damp and mould arrangements. The review identified specific weaknesses in meeting statutory Awaab's Law timescales. A recovery programme with additional approved resources is underway, with actions due by 30 September 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender considers group-level compliance failures as material governance risk; statutory non-compliance on housing safety creates regulatory exposure for the council, and recovery programmes signal unbudgeted resource deployment.","figures":"three high-risk findings, two medium-risk findings, 30 September 2026 deadline","quote":"During Q1 2026/27, an internal audit review of Damp and Mould arrangements within The Barnet Group resulted in three high-risk findings and two medium-risk findings. The review identified weaknesses in compliance with Awaab's Law timescales","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee (GARMS)","paper_title":"Appendix A - Internal Audit Q1 2026-27 progress report","paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96823/96823.pdf","headline":"Only 55% of audit actions were implemented by deadline in Q1, against a target of 90%","detail":"The council is systematically failing to implement high-priority audit recommendations on time. Of 11 high-priority actions followed up, only 3 were completed (28%), 4 were partly completed (36%), and 4 were not completed (36%). This significantly misses the 90% target and the 2025/26 full-year implementation rate of 74%, representing a persistent control environment weakness that the Head of Internal Audit has flagged as material to the annual conclusion.","category":"audit","matters":"A lender needs assurance that a council can identify and remedy control weaknesses; systematic failure to implement audit recommendations suggests the organisation cannot act on its own findings, which is a material control risk.","figures":"55%, 90%, 74%, 3 completed (28%), 4 partly completed (36%), 4 not completed (36%)","quote":"In total, 55% of actions followed up in Q1 were confirmed as implemented. This remains significantly below the Council's target of 90% and is also below the 2025/26 full-year implementation rate of 74%.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Barnet","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":true,"headline":"\u00a325m temporary borrowing raised in Q1 to support short-term cash flow","lead":"Reliance on temporary borrowing for routine cash flow suggests the council's liquid reserves or payment timing are tighter than normal","also":["24 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Children and Education Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Committee on 2026-10-08","n_findings":25,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix A - Treasury Management Performance Update Report \u2013 Q1 2627","top_paper_url":"https://barnet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96826/96826.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":82,"news_drafts_total":1}}